('Terms that matter','Plain-language reference',[
('Observation / interpretation','Observation is what was recorded. Interpretation is what it might mean. Keep them in separate fields.'),('Calibration / repeatability','Calibration compares a device against an appropriate reference. Repeatability means a method gives similar results under similar conditions; it does not prove accuracy.'),('Relative humidity / surface temperature','RH describes moisture relative to air conditions. Surface temperature is the temperature of the measured surface. They are different inputs, not interchangeable labels.'),('Confidence / evidence','Confident wording is a property of the answer. Evidence is what supports the claim. Review the latter.')]),
